+++ b/docs/V165_ACCEPTANCE_LEDGER_INTEGRITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# MASTER7 v165 acceptance ledger integrity
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.165-acceptance-ledger-integrity`
+
+## Scope
+
+v165 hardens the durable evidence used to decide whether game-provider and
+production capabilities have passed acceptance. It does not contact a provider,
+enable a payment channel, launch a game, change DNS, or open any production
+feature flag.
+
+## Durable behavior
+
+- Migration 0122 requires every acceptance history to start at revision 1 and
+  remain contiguous, and rejects updates and deletes of acceptance events.
+- PostgreSQL statement triggers reject `TRUNCATE` on both event tables and both
+  current-projection tables; readiness requires all four guards to be enabled.
+- Each current projection can only be inserted at the latest event or advanced
+  exactly one revision to the latest event; projection deletion is rejected.
+- Acceptance reads independently derive the true latest event from history and
+  fail closed when a projection is missing, stale, or points elsewhere.
+- Acceptance writes compare optimistic concurrency tokens with the true latest
+  event and refuse to write through a damaged projection.
+- PostgreSQL startup readiness requires migration 0122 and the enabled wallet
+  and acceptance-integrity triggers.
+
+## Backup and recovery
+
+The encrypted-backup schema version is `0122-acceptance-ledger-integrity`.
+The table manifest remains unchanged. An archive with the exact v164
+`0121-jdb-wager-coverage-staging` manifest remains recoverable with complete
+table coverage; altered manifests are rejected. A current production backup and
+isolated restore rehearsal are still required before readiness can pass.
+
+## Release state
+
+This document describes source code and local or isolated-database validation.
+Production acceptance, provider certification, real-money payment evidence,
+DNS cutover, activation flags, and owner sign-off remain separate fail-closed
+requirements.
